  "resultText": "I re-rendered `out/card.mp4` with the headline \"Built To Last\" and the accent color `#2F80ED`. It's still H.264, 1080x1920, 30 fps, 180 frames and exactly 6.000 s, with no audio. I checked that with ffprobe and looked at frames from the start, middle and end.\n\n- **Layout:** \"Built To\" is the white first line and \"Last\" is the blue second line. The animation, underline and moving background are unchanged.\n- **Extra color change:** I also changed the amber background glow to a light blue (`#7fb3f5`), because it was a lighter shade of the old orange accent. If you want it kept amber, set it back to `#ff9a4d` in `scenes/card.html` and re-render.\n- **Readability:** \"Last\" is hard to read while it fades in over the blue glows (around 0.7–1.2 s), as \"Faster\" was before. Once fully visible it reads clearly.\n\nFiles:\n- `out/card.mp4`\n- `scenes/card.html`\n- `scene.json`\n- `out/stills/` (new stills at 1, 2.5 and 5.9 s; `still-000.20s.png` is left over from the first version)\n- `out/export.json`",
